626 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Propositional Logic is widely used in the making rules of inference and decision making. These rules of inferences can then be used to build arguments. When several premises are given, it is hard to tell if a given argument is valid. Thus, we use these rules of inference to validate an argument and make a decision.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
627 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Example: We can prove that the following premises build up a valid argument using the rule of inference.)
