<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The compound statements whose result is always true irrespective of the intermediate result is called the tautology. In other words, the tautology is a compound statement which is always true although the individual statements can be false.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
